Today I independently identified a bug in the pmcorrect.mas method from 
"affy" package (v1.1.1), which has been posted on the mailing list before. 
But I found that the bug is still in the lastest release of affy package, 
and the results computed therefore disagree with MAS5. 


pm.corrected <- apply(cbind(pps.pm, pps.im, delta), 1, max)
  {
	...
	 pm.corrected <- apply(cbind(pps.pm, pps.im, delta), 1, max)
	...
  }

Shouldn't the above line be 

	pm.corrected <- apply(cbind(pps.pm - pps.im, delta), 1, max) 

according to the formula V_{i,j} = max(PM_{i,j} - IM_{i,j}, d) in 
Affymetrix statistical algorithm document, where PV_{i,j}= log2(V_{i,j}), 
PV_{i,j} is the probe value for probe pair j in probeset i?

Thanks,

Hongxian He
Center of Bioinformatics
University of Pennsylvania


