Hello ...

The latest version of getBioC() (1.2.28) involves a change to its
parameters and not just internal improvements.  This will not affect most
users, but for those who it will affect:

- The 'isDevel' and 'version' arguments are no longer present.
- A 'relLevel' argument has been added, which can be one of 'release',
'devel', 'contrib', and 'release1.0'.  The default is 'release', which
will always point ot the current release (currently 1.1).  The 'contrib'
option will install/update packages that have been contributed by the
Bioconductor user community.

-Jeff

