From jzhang at jimmy.harvard.edu  Tue Apr 29 09:39:55 2003
From: jzhang at jimmy.harvard.edu (John Zhang)
Date: Tue Apr 29 14:40:11 2003
Subject: [bioC] GenePlotter for mgu74v2
Message-ID: <200304291239.IAA04915@blaise.dfci.harvard.edu>

After loading the data package for mgu74a, ls(mgu74aCHRLOC) will list all the 
probe ids, get("aProbeId", mgu74aCHRLOC) will get you the chromosomal location 
for "aProbeId", and multiget("probeIds", mgu74aCHRLOC) will return a list 
containing chromosomal location data for "probeIds". Chromosomal locations are 
named by the chromosome number.

Built in information about data packages can be obtained by typing  
packageName(), ?packageName, and ?dataSetName (e.g. mgu74a(), ?mgu74a, and 
?mgu74aCHRLOC) after loading a data package.

